## Posting cadence

- `planSchedule` in `apps/server/src/publish/scheduler.ts`: each day draws 3–8 slideshows for YouTube @remedyrecoveries (`DAILY_POSTS_MIN/MAX`). Only one of those also goes to TikTok @remedy.recoveries. Stories does not get slideshows or other generated photo posts: twins are not scheduled, and `quietStoriesSlideshows` cancels any already queued on TikTok @remedy.stories or Instagram @remedy.stories. Facebook is paused, and YouTube @remedystories is paused. 8am–10pm Central, about 95+ min apart, no round minutes. TikTok @remedy.recoveries also gets that day's meme (2 posts). TikTok @remedy.stories gets the meme only. Instagram @remedy.stories does not get memes, slideshows, or Recoveries copies. Its grid is its own (`assets/ig/stories`, scheduled by `_ig-stories.ts`): closer photos, a warm grade, one small sans line, no wordmark and no white box. The boxed white caption exists only on the Stories A/B twin, which is an experiment record and is not posted.
- Windows task "Remedy Growth Autopilot" runs `scripts/autopilot.ps1` daily at 6:40am (catches up after sleep): stats pull, `schedule 7`, hand off to Zernio, then meme catch-up/retry/cancel/views. Log: `growth-engine/logs/autopilot.log`.
- Windows task "Remedy Meme Week" runs `scripts/meme-week.ps1` Sundays 8pm: one format meme a day per account group for the next 7 days, A/B on caption only. Never posts to the Remedy Recoveries Instagram, Instagram @remedy.stories, Facebook, or YouTube @remedystories. Details: `.cursor/skills/meme-make/SKILL.md`.
- Dry run: `npm run cli -w apps/server -- schedule-preview 7`. Copy check: `copy-audit` (flags slogan / non-concrete body slides).
- YouTube Shorts use the shipping beds in `assets/audio/` (the widely played Kevin MacLeod CC BY 4.0 tracks: Monkeys Spinning Monkeys, Electrodoodle, Sneaky Snitch, Fluffing a Duck, and the other beds marked `upbeat`). Credit is appended to the description. Legacy beds stay on disk only for posts that already name them. `shortBed: "none"` is the only way to post silent. Never upload a song that is not in this CC catalog.

## Main Instagram is curated (Nov 1)

`@remedyrecoveries` on Instagram is curated: only `_ig-main.ts` posts there, from a reviewed schedule. `ZERNIO_CURATED` (default `instagram:remedyrecoveries`) removes it from `accountsFor`, so the engine never auto-posts there. Those posts stay on @remedyrecoveries. They are not copied to Instagram @remedy.stories or to TikTok. Facebook and YouTube @remedystories are paused. Do not remove it from `ZERNIO_CURATED` unless the user asks.

- The grid is one look: `src/generation/ig-static.ts` (one grade on every photo, Georgia line, small REMEDY mark, bone / forest / ink cards). Plan in `assets/ig/plan.json` (posting order); render with `npx tsx src/generation/_ig-statics.ts` → `output/ig/` (posts, `grid-preview.jpg`, `captions.txt`). Look at the grid preview before posting.
- Voice (user feedback Nov 1: choppy lines read as AI): one natural sentence you would say out loud, one concrete detail, a little dry humor (Headspace calm, Duolingo setup and punchline). No two-beat fragments ("X. Your back Y."), no lists of three, no "not X but Y", no em dashes, no slogans. Captions follow the same rules.
- Purpose (user, Nov 10): both Instagram grids exist to get views, and every post is about back pain. Each line calls out a feeling people with back pain recognize (hiding it, bracing, planning a bend, being slower, feeling too young for this). No neutral object or mood lines that would fit any account ("kettle on, leaning on the counter" is out; "leaning on the counter so it looks casual" is in).
- Type-only cards are rare: about 1 in 12 posts, never two in a row. Photo posts carry the grid.
- Photos: CC0 with an entry in `assets/ig/sources.json`, or generated into `assets/ig/photos/gen/` from a `shot` (objects and places, plus the founder). The only generated person allowed is the founder, Rahul (`assets/characters/rahul/` anchor + refs), in some carousels, not all (about 1 in 4). Every photo is used once; no two slides on the grid may look alike.
- Look (user feedback Nov 1: grey, over-saturated and fake read as AI): bright, true-to-life phone color, no haze or film look. The grade only lifts dark photos; no saturation boost or contrast stretch. Founder carousels (travel, desk-day, lunch-walk, couch-desk, gym-confidence) are off the schedule until the user fixes his likeness; do not schedule founder posts without his OK. Founder shots always pass his real photos (`assets/characters/rahul/real/`) as refs and vary `hair`/`outfit`. Every generated photo, statics included, needs a `shot`. Leave plain wall or sky above his head (head below about 40% of the frame) so the Georgia line never touches him; `focus: "north"` on a slide buys a little more room.
- Carousels (`assets/ig/carousels.json`): photo cover with swipe arrow, 4 stills, then one closing slide (a library `crop_*` app slide quoting only what the screen shows, or a rare share card). `_ig-statics.ts --prompts` prints briefs for missing photos, `--import <dir> [--force]` copies them in, `--only <id>` renders one.
- Schedule: `assets/ig/schedule.json` (Central time; one static a day plus 1 to 2 carousels, odd minutes, slots vary day to day). `src/publish/_ig-main.ts --plan | --apply | --status | --cancel <id> | --page` schedules on Zernio (ids in `assets/ig/posted.json`; to swap renders, `--cancel` each id, then `--apply`, since the idempotency key hashes the rendered files) and rebuilds `apps/web/public/ig/` (https://slide.remedyrecoveries.com/ig/). On Windows run `npm run deploy` in a hidden window; wrangler flashes console windows otherwise.
- `src/publish/_ig-curate.ts --plan | --apply` lists live/scheduled posts for the handle and removes Instagram legs still queued in Zernio (backs up to `output/ig-curate/`).

